hls: play on through failed live playlist reloads, then report the error

A live playlist reload that failed once ended the playlist: reload_playlist()
returned the error, the playlist's AVIOContext took it as its end, and
hls_read_packet() treated that as the end of the stream, so a live input that
lost its server for one reload reported a clean EOF.

A reload that fails with a network error, a timeout, a server error, 429 or a
garbled answer is now retried every half target duration (at least 0.5 s)
while the segments the last load listed are played, for live_reload_timeout
(default: three target durations, at least 20 s). A client error (4xx other
than 429) fails at once. A load that fails half way leaves the playlist as it
was (it also freed nothing before: the previous segments leaked). When the
reads of a playlist end with an error, hls_read_packet() returns that error
instead of an end of stream.

